# Firebase env for react-app (Vite)

Copy to `react-app/.env.local` for local development. For GitHub Pages, set the
same names as repository Actions secrets/variables and pass them into the build.

```bash
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APPCHECK_SITE_KEY=
# Optional. GA4 measurement ID (G-…) after linking Analytics in Firebase Console.
# The SDK can also fetch this dynamically once Analytics is linked.
VITE_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID=
# Optional. Analytics is on in production builds by default. Set to 1 to test
# locally (`npm run dev`), or 0 to disable it in production.
# VITE_FIREBASE_ANALYTICS=1
```

See [docs/FIREBASE_SETUP.md](../docs/FIREBASE_SETUP.md). Without these, the app
runs in local-only mode (sessionStorage + .scrkpr import/export).
